etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4176036\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: khou.com\nSLUG: 507-c96c4235-0cc2-4573-b720-8b95f5741121\nTEXT: NASA\'s Artemis III mission is set to launch in November 2026, with astronauts Mike Hopkins and Mark Vande Hei leading the crew. The mission aims to land on the lunar south pole, with a focus on exploring the region\'s resources and testing technologies for future human missions to Mars. The crew will spend several weeks on the lunar surface, conducting scientific experiments and gathering data on the moon\'s geology and composition. The mission will also test NASA\'s Space Launch System (SLS) rocket and Orion spacecraft, which are designed to take humans beyond Earth\'s orbit.\n\nID: 4176035\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: khou.com\nSLUG: 507-a81afb44-8f6c-44f6-a77a-52399c02a75c\nTEXT: NASA\'s Artemis III mission aims to land the first woman and the next man on the lunar surface by 2025. The crew will include astronauts Mike Hopkins, Mark Vande Hei and Jessica Watkins. The mission will test the Space Launch System (SLS) rocket and the Orion spacecraft, which will travel more than 26,000 miles to the Moon. The lunar lander, developed by SpaceX, will be used for the first time on a NASA mission. The crew will spend about 26 hours on the lunar surface, collecting samples and conducting scientific experiments.\n\n\n',)
