etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4173092\nCREATED: 2026-06-08\nDOMAIN: globalnews.ca\nSLUG: icc-chief-prosecutor-suspended-karim-khan\nTEXT: Karim Khan, the chief prosecutor of the International Criminal Court, has been suspended from his duties after being referred for disciplinary proceedings by the court\'s oversight body. The suspension comes amid allegations of sexual misconduct with a female aide, which Khan has denied. A UN investigation found evidence of non-consensual sexual contact with the aide in various locations, including his office and private residence. However, a panel of judicial experts advised that the investigation was not conclusive enough to make a final decision on Khan\'s fate. The Assembly of States Parties, the court\'s oversight body, will now hold a special session to decide whether Khan can remain in his job at the global court.\n\nID: 4172914\nCREATED: 2026-06-08\nDOMAIN: boston25news.com\nSLUG: fleqqdboim7krm6vvlt3llolwq\nTEXT: Karim Khan, the chief prosecutor of the International Criminal Court, has been suspended pending a decision by the Assembly of States Parties over allegations of sexual misconduct. The suspension comes after a UN investigation found evidence of non-consensual sexual contact with a female aide, including in Khan\'s office and private residence. The investigation was conducted by the Office of Internal Oversight Services (OIOS) and reviewed written submissions from experts. A final decision on Khan\'s fate is now up to the Assembly of States Parties, which will hold a special session to determine if he can remain in his job at the global court.\n\n\n',)
