etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4173363\nCREATED: 2026-06-08\nDOMAIN: interestingengineering.com\nSLUG: airbus-u145-autonomous-helicopter-drone\nTEXT: Airbus Unveils U145 Autonomous Helicopter Drone. \n\nAirbus has unveiled the U145, an autonomous helicopter drone designed for various applications such as search and rescue, surveillance, and cargo transport. The U145 features advanced autonomous capabilities, including a 360-degree vision system and a sophisticated navigation system. The drone is equipped with a modular design, allowing for easy integration of various payloads and sensors. Airbus aims to utilize the U145 in a range of industries, including energy, transportation, and emergency services.\n\nID: 4173330\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: twz.com\nSLUG: airbus-unveils-u145-uncrewed-cargo-helicopter\nTEXT: Airbus has unveiled the U145, an uncrewed cargo helicopter offering a mission-agnostic solution for civil and military applications. The U145 combines the airframe, power, and useful load of its H145 helicopter counterpart with autonomy. CEO Matthieu Louvot stated that the U145 will have a maximum takeoff weight of 8,400 pounds and a payload capacity of up to 2,600 pounds. In comparison, the uncrewed MQ-72C Lakota Connector can carry a maximum payload of around 4,000 pounds.\n\n\n',)
