etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4173230\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: scrippsnews.com\nSLUG: donald-trump-arrives-at-game-3-of-the-nba-finals-the-1st-sitting-us-president-to-attend\nTEXT: Donald Trump arrived at Game 3 of the NBA Finals, becoming the first sitting US President to attend a major sporting event. The security measures in place have caused significant hassles for fans, with thousands missing the start of last year\'s US Open men\'s singles final due to lengthy security lines. The added screening measures have also led to fans having to go through multiple checks, including when arriving at the Billie Jean King National Tennis Center and again in front of Arthur Ashe Stadium, where Trump watched from a suite. The high ticket prices for Knicks fans have made it difficult to attend the game in-person, with some paying over $5,000 for a ticket.\n\nID: 4175484\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: apnews.com\nSLUG: trump-knicks-jinx-home-team-05b2acc879ffb3fc86920535d5231047\nTEXT: Donald Trump\'s presence at a New York Knicks game led to long and loud boos from the crowd, with frequent booing not keeping him away. Knicks fan Stephen Smith blamed Trump for disrupting the team\'s "mojo", to which Trump responded, saying he thinks Smith lacks the intelligence to run for president. This incident is not a new one, as Trump has faced similar boos at other events, including Nationals\' and Commanders\' games. The White House attempted to spin the incident as a show of strength, while the Daily News tabloid featured a cartoon depicting an exaggeratedly rotund Trump wearing a Knicks jersey with a declining approval rating.\n\nID: 4173073\nCREATED: 2026-06-08\nDOMAIN: deseret.com\nSLUG: stephen-a-smith-sounds-off-on-trump-attending-nba-finals-at-msg\nTEXT: Stephen A. Smith sounded off on President Donald Trump attending Game 3 of the NBA Finals at Madison Square Garden, calling it a "big mistake". Smith, a longtime Knicks fan, believes Trump\'s presence will overshadow the game and create security issues. He stated that Trump\'s decision to attend is "ridiculous" and will make the game "unwatchable". Smith also expressed his disappointment that Trump\'s appearance will lead to increased security measures, which will prevent fans from watching the game outside of the Garden.\n\n\n',)
