etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4173344\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: hyperallergic.com\nSLUG: winning-penn-station-redesign-features-trumps-name\nTEXT: The redesigned Penn Station will feature a Beaux-Arts-inspired exterior with large American flags, gold-colored bronze railings, and a terracotta city skyline. The exterior will also include an eagle figure on the entrance facade and a presidential seal with President Trump\'s name etched into a wall near the entrance. The design was selected after a competitive process and is being developed by Penn Transformation Partners, a group of private companies and designers led by Vornado and Halmar.\n\nID: 4175471\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: apnews.com\nSLUG: new-york-penn-station-trump-reconstruction-7b2eb6ca8f1f32ad591b52066edc59a8\nTEXT: A new vision for New York\'s Penn Station aims to restore its grandeur from 1910. Renderings released Monday feature a rectangular stone facade with imposing columns, a grand entryway and soaring ceilings over 50 feet high in some areas. The design includes bronze finishes, ornamental details such as a bas-relief of the city\'s skyline and a large station clock.\n\n\n',)
