etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4175963\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: antaranews.com\nSLUG: bi-rate-hike-boosts-investor-confidence-as-rupiah-rebounds\nTEXT: Indonesia\'s central bank, Bank Indonesia (BI), has raised interest rates to defend the rupiah, which has rebounded following severe external pressure. Minister Airlangga emphasized that the country\'s core economic fundamentals remain robust, driven by strong export performance and solid macroeconomic indicators. Data from the Central Statistics Agency (BPS) shows the Indonesian economy grew 5.61% year-on-year in Q1 2026. The minister noted that Indonesia\'s agricultural sector is uniquely secure, with the country exporting approximately 1.5 million tons of urea to regional countries. This stability is expected to support the rupiah exchange rate, which is forecasted to strengthen to Rp16,800-17,500 per US dollar in 2027.\n\nID: 4175465\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: businesstimes.com.sg\nSLUG: bank-indonesias-emergency-rate-hike-buys-time-battered-rupiah-investor-doubts-linger\nTEXT: Bank Indonesia\'s surprise emergency rate hike may buy the battered rupiah some breathing room, but it also reveals the conundrum facing policymakers as external shocks, capital outflows and investor unease over policies collide in South-east Asia\'s largest economy. The central bank raised its benchmark seven-day reverse repo rate by 25 basis points (bps) to 5.5 per cent on Tuesday, in an unscheduled move that analysts described as necessary to defend the rupiah after it became one of the world\'s worst-performing emerging-market currencies this year, amid growing global volatility from the conflict in the Middle East.\n\nID: 4176083\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: hurriyetdailynews.com\nSLUG: indonesias-central-bank-unveils-surprise-rate-hike-to-stem-rupiah-rout-223071\nTEXT: Indonesia\'s Central Bank Unveils Surprise Rate Hike to Stem Rupiah Rout. The central bank lifted borrowing costs to 5.5 percent, following an unexpected 50-point increase last month aimed at stabilizing the weakening rupiah and battling inflation. The move came ahead of its next monthly monetary policy meeting, a week away. Jakarta\'s main stock index rose nearly five percent in Tuesday morning trade. The rupiah has fallen to more than 18,000 to the dollar, a record low, stung by surging energy costs.\n\nID: 4175766\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: asiaone.com\nSLUG: indonesia-hikes-rates-surprise-cycle-move-prop-sinking-rupiah\nTEXT: Indonesia hikes interest rates in a surprise move, causing the rupiah to sink. Barclays predicts that if the rupiah stabilizes, Indonesia may start making cuts. BI Governor Perry Warjiyo stated that the country\'s foreign exchange reserves are "more than enough" to stabilize the currency. Warjiyo also said that the bank\'s policy aims to increase returns by attracting foreign portfolio investment inflows, with projected rupiah rates of 16,800 to 17,500 to the dollar in 2027.\n\n\n',)
