etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4175547\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: thedailystar.net\nSLUG: world-conflicts-hit-peak-2025-4195036\nTEXT: The World Conflict Data Program, attached to Uppsala University, has released a study revealing that conflicts reached their peak in 2025. Africa was the most affected region, with 29 conflicts involving at least one state. Israel was identified as a country with high levels of aggression, involved in conflicts in Gaza, Syria, Lebanon, against Iran, and against Houthi rebels. The US was also highlighted as a country with increasing violence under President Donald Trump\'s return to power, leading to trade barriers and a more polarized world.\n\nID: 4176114\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: hurriyetdailynews.com\nSLUG: world-conflicts-hit-peak-in-2025-report-223076\nTEXT: The world has experienced a peak in conflicts in 2025, with only two years since the Cold War\'s end surpassing this bloodshed. The Rwanda genocide in 1994 and the war in Ethiopia\'s Tigray region in 2021 were the most recent examples. This year, multiple large-scale conflicts have overlapped and taken turns on each other.\n\n\n',)
