etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4175689\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: smh.com.au\nSLUG: belfast-police-arrest-man-after-brutal-attempted-beheading-20260609-p605cm-html\nTEXT: A Sudanese asylum seeker has been charged with attempted murder after a brutal stabbing attack in Belfast left a man fighting for his life. The incident, which was captured on graphic video, showed the assailant kneeling over the victim and yelling while brandishing a knife above his head. The attack sparked violent protests against migration, with hundreds gathering in Belfast and other cities to demand action. Anti-immigration groups called for rallies across the UK, leading conservative leaders to call for the police to reveal the suspect\'s ethnicity and details of the victim\'s injuries. The protests turned violent, with a bus set alight in East Belfast and crowds of 100 men kicking in doors and breaking windows of homes on a nearby street.\n\nID: 4175628\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: foxnews.com\nSLUG: bystanders-hailed-heroic-after-intervening-brutal-knife-attack-sudanese-migrant-uk\nTEXT: Bystanders are being hailed as heroic after intervening in a brutal knife attack by a Sudanese migrant in the UK. The incident occurred on Monday evening, with witnesses describing the scene as "chaotic" and "terrifying". The victim, a local resident, was reportedly stabbed multiple times before the bystanders stepped in to stop the attack. The suspects, who are believed to be asylum seekers, were taken into custody by police. The incident has sparked outrage and concern about the safety of asylum seekers in the UK, with some calling for increased security measures.\n\nID: 4175637\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: scmp.com\nSLUG: suspect-arrested-sickening-belfast-stabbing-attack-videos-spread-online\nTEXT: A Sudanese man was arrested in connection with a stabbing attack in Belfast, Northern Ireland. The victim, whose face, neck, and back were seriously injured, was taken to the hospital late on Monday. The incident drew national attention due to graphic videos of the attack spreading online. UK Prime Minister Keir Starmer\'s office appealed for calm, following the arrest of the suspect.\n\n\n',)
