etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4175946\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: tempo.co\nSLUG: japanese-city-captures-black-bear-after-multi-day-hunt\nTEXT: Authorities in Utsunomiya, north of Tokyo, captured a wild black bear after a multi-day hunt. The bear was estimated to weigh around 100 kilograms (220 pounds) and had been spotted near a library, shopping arcade, university campus, and market. The city closed all 94 public schools and urged residents to stay indoors after the bear was first spotted on Saturday evening. The bear resurfaced again near a private home on Tuesday, prompting police to cordone off the area and shoot it with a tranquilizer gun. The city is yet to decide what to do with the bear, and authorities have reported a possible second bear roaming around. This incident is part of a larger spike in casualties from bear encounters in Japan, with 13 people killed by bears last year.\n\nID: 4175424\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: channelnewsasia.com\nSLUG: japan-bear-caught-utsunomiya-school-closures-6171226\nTEXT: A bear was caught in Utsunomiya after forcing the closure of 94 public primary and middle schools due to sightings. The bear was tranquilized with a third shot, which successfully hit the animal. It is unclear if there were multiple bears roaming the city. In a separate incident, an "extremely intelligent" bear in Fukushima injured four people and remains at large. The recent surge in bear sightings is attributed to a jump in animal activity as they emerge from hibernation, seeking food due to an abundance of food sources under a warming climate.\n\nID: 4176133\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: mainichi.jp\nSLUG: 002000c\nTEXT: A 100-kg bear was caught after four days of sightings in Utsunomiya, Tochigi Prefecture, north of Tokyo. The bear was spotted in a residential area on June 9, 2026, prompting its capture.\n\n\n',)
