etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4175803\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: boston25news.com\nSLUG: 4s4myow56y2ulbbjyifirz5i6m\nTEXT: A US journalist, Rohde, was sentenced to life in prison for his role in a kidnapping plot. He had set up an interview with Najibullah, who was behind the killing of three US soldiers. Rohde claimed he was a journalist trying to get the viewpoint of a Taliban commander, but Najibullah\'s cohorts claimed he was a spy. The judge rejected most of the defense lawyer\'s arguments for leniency, citing Najibullah\'s guilty plea and harsh prison conditions. The judge praised Rohde for his work on behalf of families affected by kidnappings, but noted that he had made a "biggest mistake" in setting up the interview.\n\nID: 4176050\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: thestar.com\nSLUG: article-061c05dd-eb99-51c2-b4a7-43d15fae2f27-html\nTEXT: A Taliban commander, Najibullah, has been sentenced to 42 years in prison for the killings of US soldiers and journalists, as well as kidnappings. The judge praised Rohde, a former Taliban commander who turned informant, for his work on behalf of the families of kidnapped victims. Rohde described setting up an interview with Najibullah as "the biggest mistake of my life" and claimed he would not have done it if he knew Najibullah was behind the killings. The judge rejected most of the arguments for leniency made by Najibullah\'s defense lawyer, who portrayed him as protecting his homeland during war.\n\nID: 4175449\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: apnews.com\nSLUG: taliban-commander-sentencing-reporter-rohde-993db6a6404b7451fbd7956f3c0db313\nTEXT: A Taliban commander, Najibullah, was sentenced to 10 years in prison for his role in the kidnapping of three American soldiers. The judge praised Rohde, a journalist who set up an interview with Najibullah, for his work on behalf of the families of other kidnapped victims. Rohde described the interview as "the biggest mistake of my life" and said he would not have done it if he knew Najibullah was behind the killing. The defense lawyer argued for an 18-year prison term, but the judge rejected most of these arguments.\n\n\n',)
