etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4175418\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: channelnewsasia.com\nSLUG: rescuers-race-reach-trapped-victims-after-powerful-quake-in-southern-philippines-6171276\nTEXT: Rescue efforts are underway after a powerful 7.8-magnitude earthquake struck off the coast of Sarangani province in the southern Philippines on Monday, killing at least 37 people and injuring over 400. The worst-hit city, General Santos, was left with debris, toppled power lines and damaged infrastructure. Strong aftershocks forced residents to spend the night in evacuation centers and tents, with authorities placing General Santos under a state of calamity. Emergency crews are working to restore power and water services, while tsunami warnings were triggered across several countries, including Mindanao and Manado in Indonesia.\n\nID: 4175878\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: tempo.co\nSLUG: philippines-large-mindanao-quake-displaced-roughly-20000\nTEXT: A magnitude 7.8 earthquake displaced over 20,000 people in the Philippines, particularly in Mindanao\'s southern coast. The epicenter was just off General Santos city, where 13 people were killed in collapsed buildings or by falling debris. In Glan, a landslide buried several houses, claiming 18 lives in Sarangani province. The quake also damaged around 2,000 houses and 117 government buildings across several provinces. General Santos\' international airport was shut, forcing the cancellation of 63 domestic flights.\n\nID: 4176058\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: japantimes.co.jp\nSLUG: outdoor-hospitals-philippines-quake-toll\nTEXT: The death toll from a magnitude-7.8 earthquake in the Philippines has risen to 40, with thousands displaced and over 450 injured. In General Santos, doctors treated patients in tents under the scorching sun, including a young mother who gave birth. The earthquake struck off Mindanao island on Monday, with four people now believed missing. In Sarangani province, some areas remain inaccessible by land due to damage, and rescue efforts are hindered by fears of aftershocks.\n\nID: 4176086\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: hurriyetdailynews.com\nSLUG: outdoor-hospitals-shaken-communities-as-philippine-quake-toll-rises-223073\nTEXT: The Philippine earthquake has left 223,073 people affected, with many communities severely impacted. Infrastructure damage is widespread, causing roads to be impassable for at least a week due to bridge collapses. In Glan municipality, a landslide buried 13 people in their homes. At another hospital, staff reported over 60 patients were forced to sleep on beds outside due to concerns about the building\'s structural integrity.\n\nID: 4175896\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: tempo.co\nSLUG: todays-top-3-news-impact-of-philippines-quake-on-indonesia\nTEXT: A powerful 7.8 magnitude earthquake struck the southern Philippines on June 8, 2026, causing at least 31 deaths and 12 missing persons. The earthquake occurred off the coast of Sarangani province at 7:37 am local time, resulting in extensive damage and disruption of services. Buildings collapsed, power and water services were disrupted, and landslides triggered in some areas.\n\nID: 4175603\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: ctvnews.ca\nSLUG: 32000-people-displaced-by-the-philippine-earthquake-that-killed-at-least-37\nTEXT: At least 37 people have been killed and 32,000 displaced by a Philippine earthquake. The disaster occurred in the Philippines, causing widespread destruction and displacement.\n\n\n',)
