etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4175933\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: thenationalnews.com\nSLUG: president-sheikh-mohamed-receives-presidential-camel-racing-team-in-abu-dhabi\nTEXT: President Sheikh Mohamed received the Presidential Camel Racing Team in Abu Dhabi on Tuesday, where he reviewed their achievements over the 2025-2026 season. The team won in the King Abdulaziz Camel Festival, Oman\'s Al Etihad Festival and Al Bashayer Festival, Kuwait International Camel Racing Championship, and season-closing festivals in Al Marmoom and Al Shahaniya. After congratulating the team, Sheikh Mohamed emphasized that camel racing is an integral part of the UAE\'s cultural heritage and reflects society\'s deep connection to its values and traditions.\n\nID: 4177414\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: gulftoday.ae\nSLUG: president-reviews-camel-racing-teams-achievements\nTEXT: Sheikh Mohamed congratulated the Presidential Camel Racing Team on their achievements, praising their efforts to enhance performance and competitiveness. He emphasized the importance of preserving this national heritage for future generations. Members of a delegation expressed appreciation for Sheikh Mohamed\'s support, noting it strengthened their ability to participate in competitions at home and abroad. The UAE\'s integrated sports infrastructure, including Yas Marina Circuit and Hazza Bin Zayed Stadium, has become a key pillar in advancing sporting excellence.\n\n\n',)
