etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4177225\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: asiaone.com\nSLUG: 32000-people-displaced-philippine-earthquake-killed-least-37\nTEXT: At least 37 people have been killed and 32,000 displaced in a Philippine earthquake that struck on Monday. The quake was centered at sea, 33 kilometers deep and approximately 32 kilometers southwest of Maasim town in Sarangani province. The Philippine Institute of Volcanology and Seismology reported that the earthquake was triggered by movement in the Cotabato Trench, similar to a 1976 quake that caused widespread destruction and resulted in the deaths of approximately 8,000 people. President Ferdinand Marcos Jr. deployed defense-mitigation officials to oversee search and rescue efforts, distribute food packs and construction materials, and assess damage to infrastructure.\n\nID: 4177101\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: ocregister.com\nSLUG: philippines-earthquake-strikes-mindanao-causing-deaths\nTEXT: Rescuers in the southern Philippines searched ruined buildings on Tuesday to ensure no one was trapped after a 7.8 magnitude earthquake killed at least 37 people and displaced over 32,000. The earthquake centered off Mindanao injured nearly 500 people and many fled to emergency shelters, fearing a tsunami. Waves up to 1.4-meters above tide level were measured in the Philippines, but only six shanties on stilts in a coastal village reported tsunami damage. Rescuers installed tents as they prepared for a search operation, with four people considered missing on official records.\n\nID: 4177511\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: geo.tv\nSLUG: 668037-death-toll-from-philippines-quake-rises-to-46\nTEXT: The death toll from the Philippines earthquake has risen to 45, with most of the additional fatalities coming from Davao Occidental province. Most were killed in landslides or collapsing buildings, according to civil defence official Rafaelito Alejandro. The national disaster agency reported a jump in missing persons from four to 17, but the figure did not include the newly confirmed fatality of Joey Deluvio, a 39-year-old supermarket employee found pinned between two beams.\n\nID: 4176058\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: japantimes.co.jp\nSLUG: outdoor-hospitals-philippines-quake-toll\nTEXT: The death toll from a magnitude-7.8 earthquake in the Philippines has risen to 40, with thousands displaced and over 450 injured. In General Santos, doctors treated patients in tents under the scorching sun, including a young mother who gave birth. The earthquake struck off Mindanao island on Monday, with four people now believed missing. In Sarangani province, some areas remain inaccessible by land due to damage, and rescue efforts are hindered by fears of aftershocks.\n\nID: 4177122\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: manilatimes.net\nSLUG: 2362330\nTEXT: A 7.8-magnitude earthquake in Mindanao has displaced over 32,000 people, prompting the Philippine Seismological Institute to commemorate the anniversary of a similar 1976 quake and tsunami. The disaster has left thousands injured, with extensive damages reported in northern provinces and cities. President Ferdinand Marcos Jr. has deployed officials from Manila to oversee search and rescue efforts, food distribution, and infrastructure assessment.\n\nID: 4177051\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: fakti.bg\nSLUG: 1060048-after-the-earthquake-in-the-philippines-45-dead-17-missing-630-injured\nTEXT: The death toll from the 7.8-magnitude earthquake in Mindanao island has reached 45, with 17 missing and 630 injured. Search, rescue and relief operations are being carried out in extremely difficult conditions due to continuous aftershocks. Most of the victims are buried under the rubble of collapsed buildings or caught in mudslides triggered by the earthquake in Sarangani province.\n\nID: 4176884\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: thedailystar.net\nSLUG: death-toll-philippines-quake-rises-46-4195126\nTEXT: The death toll from the Philippines earthquake has risen to 45, with 17 people still missing. The majority of additional fatalities were from Davao Occidental province, where most were killed in landslides or collapsing buildings.\n\n\n',)
