etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4176919\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: apnews.com\nSLUG: albania-rama-trump-kushner-development-protests-767df9dc0a359c0357a502b5c49f2aa5\nTEXT: Albanian Prime Minister Edi Rama is pushing forward with a luxury development linked to Donald Trump\'s son-in-law Jared Kushner, despite protests over its environmental impact. The project, which includes hotels, apartments, villas, and a marina for yachts, has sparked daily demonstrations outside Rama\'s office in Tirana. The government claims the development will transform Albania into a high-end tourism destination and boost European Union membership, but Rama dismissed environmental concerns as misinformation. An investigation has been launched by Albania\'s anti-corruption agency, amid rival claims over the land\'s privatization.\n\nID: 4177112\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: ocregister.com\nSLUG: albania-prime-minister-kushner-luxury-tourism-project-protests\nTEXT: Albania\'s Prime Minister Rama has dismissed environmental objections to his luxury tourism project, claiming they are based on misinformation. The project, which includes hotels, apartments, villas, and a marina for yachts, is seen as transformational for the country\'s economy. However, thousands of protesters have joined daily demonstrations outside Rama\'s office in Tirana against the project. The government claims the land is privately owned, but rival claims over its privatization have emerged. An investigation has been opened by Albania\'s anti-corruption agency, and protesters took to the streets in Tirana on June 9, 2026.\n\n\n',)
