etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4176785\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: news18.com\nSLUG: pm-modi-longest-serving-elected-prime-minister-india-nda-conclave-bharat-mandapam-12-years-modi-government-record-ws-l-10139723-html\nTEXT: Prime Minister Narendra Modi has become India\'s longest-serving elected Prime Minister, surpassing Jawaharlal Nehru\'s record of 4,399 consecutive days in office. The achievement will be formally recognized at a National Democratic Alliance (NDA) conclave in New Delhi, where senior leaders will honor Modi\'s tenure and review the government\'s future priorities. The meeting, scheduled at Bharat Mandapam, will bring together chief ministers and senior leaders from 22 NDA-ruled states and Union Territories. The NDA is expected to pass a resolution congratulating Modi on achieving the historic feat, while discussions will also focus on flagship welfare schemes, major infrastructure projects, and efforts to ensure benefits reach the last mile.\n\nID: 4176706\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: lokmattimes.com\nSLUG: ministers-hail-pm-modi-as-he-completes-4399-days-sets-tenure-record-2\nTEXT: PM Modi completes 12 years as Prime Minister and sets a record for India\'s longest-serving elected PM. Union Minister Hardeep Singh praises Modi\'s achievements in economic growth, digital transformation, infrastructure expansion, and social empowerment. The government\'s flagship programmes, such as Swachh Bharat Mission and Smart Cities Mission, reflect its focus on inclusive development and citizen welfare. Modi\'s vision of a "Viksit Bharat" aims to ensure dignity, opportunity, and hope for every citizen by 2047.\n\nID: 4176713\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: lokmattimes.com\nSLUG: pm-modi-became-prime-minister-through-peoples-mandate-not-privilege-union-minister-giriraj-singh\nTEXT: Union Minister Giriraj Singh stated that Prime Minister Narendra Modi became India\'s longest-serving democratically elected Prime Minister through the people\'s mandate, not privilege. This was highlighted during celebrations marking 12 years of Modi\'s government at the Centre, where he offered prayers at a Hanuman temple. Singh praised Modi\'s journey and contributions to the country, noting his rise to the highest elected office was due to popular support rather than privilege.\n\nID: 4176783\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: news18.com\nSLUG: pm-modi-12-years-prime-minister-public-service-good-governance-longest-serving-prime-minister-nda-meeting-ws-l-10140146-html\nTEXT: Prime Minister Narendra Modi marked a record-breaking 12 years in office, becoming India\'s longest-serving Prime Minister. In a post on X, Modi emphasized the importance of public service as the ultimate measure of good governance. He stressed that humility, dedication, and a strong sense of duty are essential to earning the trust of the people. This marks 4,399 days in office, surpassing former Prime Minister Jawaharlal Nehru\'s record of 4,398 consecutive days.\n\n\n',)
