etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4176887\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: indiatoday.in\nSLUG: indian-army-procurement-300-k9-vajra-artillery-guns-rs-23000-crore-defence-procurement-board-meet-this-week-2924375-2026-06-10\nTEXT: The Indian Army is set to acquire 300 K9 Vajra artillery guns worth Rs 23,000 crore as part of its efforts to strengthen long-range firepower. The proposed acquisition would significantly expand the Army\'s artillery inventory, taking the total number of K9 Vajra guns ordered by India to over 500. The system, capable of engaging targets at ranges exceeding 40 kilometres, offers armoured protection and high mobility, enabling deployment in both desert and mountainous regions. The Army\'s confidence in the system has been reinforced by its operational performance over the past several years, with trials of a modified cold-weather variant conducted successfully in Ladakh.\n\nID: 4176780\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: news18.com\nSLUG: indian-army-eyes-major-artillery-boost-plans-to-procure-300-more-k9-vajra-guns-ws-l-10139785-html\nTEXT: The Indian Army is planning to acquire 300 more K9 Vajra-T self-propelled howitzers, worth around Rs 23,000 crore. The Defence Procurement Board is expected to review the proposal in the coming days. This acquisition would be one of the largest artillery procurement programmes undertaken by the Army in recent decades, significantly strengthening India\'s long-range firepower across both the western and northern borders.\n\n\n',)
