etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4175944\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: tempo.co\nSLUG: survey-prabowos-approval-falls-to-59-8-as-economic-concerns-grow\nTEXT: Prabowo\'s approval rating falls to 59.8% as economic concerns grow, with respondents citing price increases of basic necessities and unemployment as main reasons for dissatisfaction. \n\nAccording to the survey, 34.14% of respondents who expressed dissatisfaction with Prabowo\'s performance mentioned the increase in prices of basic necessities as the main reason, while 15.76% attributed it to minimal job opportunities and high unemployment among young people. \n\nThe survey also found that 48.21% of respondents assessed the national economic conditions to be just average, while 16.1% believed them to be good and 35.69% stated they were poor. \n\nThe majority of respondents, or 49.51%, indicated that their family\'s economic conditions have not changed compared to a year ago, while 18.21% stated that the weakening of the rupiah\'s exchange rate has a significant impact on their economic conditions. \n\n53.5% of respondents admitted that the increase in the price of BBM has significantly affected their economy, with 77.8% disagreeing with increasing the price of BBM. \n\nThe survey was conducted on 1,230 respondents in 38 provinces from May 26 to June 1, 2026.\n\nID: 4175852\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: cbs8.com\nSLUG: 509-5366b49f-1b81-4044-b745-736e852419b4\nTEXT: Vista Company Launches Innovative Lighting Solution. \n\nThe Vista Company, a leading provider of smart home solutions, has developed an innovative lighting system that utilizes more natural daylight and less electricity to illuminate homes. \n\nThis new technology, designed for residential use, reduces energy consumption by up to 75% compared to traditional lighting systems. \n\nBy harnessing the power of natural light, homes can save on energy bills and reduce their carbon footprint. \n\nThe system\'s advanced sensors detect the amount of natural light available in a room and adjust the lighting accordingly, ensuring optimal brightness and energy efficiency. \n\nThis cutting-edge solution is expected to revolutionize the way homes are lit, making it a more sustainable and cost-effective option for homeowners.\n\n\n',)
