etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4168678\nCREATED: 2026-06-07\nDOMAIN: channelnewsasia.com\nSLUG: china-gaokao-students-examination-university-6167211\nTEXT: China\'s National College Entrance Examination (NCEE) or "gaokao" has seen a shift in attitudes, with students and parents becoming more willing to prioritize physical and mental health over high test scores. Mothers and fathers, dressed in red for good fortune, cluster outside exam halls, while police and security guards are on high alert to prevent cheating. The education authorities have explicitly warned students not to bring smart glasses or watches into test sites, which are surveilled by video. This year\'s exams feature topics of change and adapting to challenges, such as an artificial intelligence event for retirees. Students are asked to write slogans for the event or 800 words about technology\'s impact on human imagination. Despite this, many students still aim to achieve their dream of attending a top university, but some are becoming more cautious and prioritizing mental well-being.\n\nID: 4168270\nCREATED: 2026-06-07\nDOMAIN: globaltimes.cn\nSLUG: 1362931-shtml\nTEXT: China Central Television reports that AI monitoring systems in examination rooms can automatically flag unusual behavior by candidates or invigilators, generating video clips for further review. This technology is being utilized during the annual gaokao season, China\'s college entrance examination period, to enhance fairness and accuracy.\n\n\n',)
