etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4166825\nCREATED: 2026-06-06\nDOMAIN: tempo.co\nSLUG: explore-jakarta-4-festivals-to-brighten-up-your-weekend\nTEXT: The National Gallery of Indonesia in Central Jakarta is hosting the "Panoramica" exhibition, featuring works by Uruguayan artists Luis Fabini and Manuel Rodríguez, to commemorate the 60th anniversary of diplomatic relations between Indonesia and Uruguay. The exhibition runs from June 5-28, 2026, with ticket prices ranging from Rp25,000 to Rp50,000. \n\nIn Central Jakarta, the 2026 Jakarta Future Festival (JFF) is taking place from June 5-7, 2026. The event features discussions on "Navigating Resilience" and includes two programs: the Jakarta Forecast and The Urban Talks. \n\nIn East Jakarta, the National Keris Exhibition is being held from May 23-June 28, 2026. The exhibition showcases a diverse collection of keris and serves as an educational space for the historical, philosophical, and artistic value of keris-making. \n\nIn Central Jakarta, the TMII Heritage Museum is hosting an event with a weather forecast indicating thick clouds in Jakarta.\n\nID: 4162810\nCREATED: 2026-06-05\nDOMAIN: antaranews.com\nSLUG: indonesia-uruguay-mark-60-years-of-ties-with-panoramica-exhibition\nTEXT: The Embassy of Uruguay in Indonesia, in collaboration with the Culture Ministry and the National Gallery of Indonesia, is hosting an exhibition titled "Panoramica" to celebrate 60 years of ties between the two countries. The exhibition, featuring works by Uruguayan artists Luis Fabini and Manuel Rodriguez, explores different perspectives on landscapes and the relationship between humans and nature. The event will take place from June 5 to 28, 2026 at Building D of the National Gallery in Jakarta.\n\n\n',)
