etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4158506\nCREATED: 2026-06-04\nDOMAIN: apnews.com\nSLUG: venice-biennale-protest-russia-israel-golden-lion-0d1c92d173c530e63b146f1c3dd27063\nTEXT: The Venice Biennale has faced a protest over its handling of the Golden Lion prize, with some 70 artists and nearly 40 national pavilions calling for Russia to be barred from returning due to its invasion of Ukraine. The protest letter, which cited investigations by the International Criminal Court, claimed that Russia and Israel were singled out for their involvement in crimes against humanity. In response, the Biennale stated it would keep all names on the ballot to guarantee visitor freedom of expression, but none would be considered for prizes. Austrian artist Florentina Holzinger\'s exhibition, featuring recycled waste water from portable toilets outside the Austrian Pavilion, was one of the most popular at the Biennale.\n\nID: 4156531\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nDOMAIN: theartnewspaper.com\nSLUG: venice-verdicts-art-world-figures-give-their-thoughts-on-the-2026-biennale\nTEXT: The 2026 Venice Biennale has sparked controversy with over 70 artists withdrawing from awards in protest. The withdrawal is a response to the resignation of the exhibition\'s jury, with notable artists such as Walid Raad, Alice Maher, and Alfredo Jaar signing a protest statement in solidarity. In contrast, Khaled Sabsabi\'s work will be featured in both the main Venice Biennale show and the cancelled Australia Pavilion, marking a "major historic first" for an Australian artist.\n\n\n',)
