etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4176499\nCREATED: 2026-06-08\nDOMAIN: prnewswire.com\nSLUG: cerave-wituje-sukces-ponad-100-nagrodzonych-tworcow-treci-z-22-krajow-1-globalna-edycja-cerawards-302794006-html\nTEXT: CeraVe\'s Global Edition of the CerAwards has celebrated over 100 creators from 22 countries, with a special event in Hollywood. The initiative aims to push the boundaries of storytelling, spark creativity and redefine possibilities at the intersection of content creation, education and entertainment. Dr. Andrew Park, a certified dermatologist and internet creator, notes that CeraVe has been at the forefront of utilizing social media to increase skin health education and was a pioneer in engaging dermatologists in conversations on the topic. The company, founded in 2005, collaborates with dermatologists to develop products that support skin repair and maintenance. CeraVe\'s products, featuring three identical ceramides found naturally in the skin (AP, NP and EOP), are available in over 60 countries worldwide.\n\nID: 4167822\nCREATED: 2026-06-05\nDOMAIN: prnewswire.com\nSLUG: cerave-feiert-uber-100-preisgekronte-content-schopfer-aus-22-landern-bei-den-ersten-globalen-cerawards-302792830-html\nTEXT: CeraVe celebrates over 100 prize-winning content creators from 22 countries at the first-ever Global Cera Awards. The brand, founded in 2005 with the goal of offering therapeutic skin care for all, has contributed to the development of dermatologists, health experts, and creatives engaging in social media. Vincent Chauvière, Global Brand President of CeraVe, stated that the brand has always targeted where culture happens and was one of the first to utilize social media platforms to make dermatological awareness more appealing and accessible. The Global Cera Awards will bring together 111 creatives from 22 countries for a unique Hollywood experience, aiming to redefine what is possible when creativity, science, and entertainment come together.\n\n\n',)
