etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4162759\nCREATED: 2026-06-05\nDOMAIN: khou.com\nSLUG: 507-034df1ef-c7a8-4a1c-b34b-bb3a0779427e\nTEXT: Marjane Satrapi, a French-Iranian artist and author, has been recognized for her advocacy on human rights in Iran. In 2023, she coordinated a book project "Femme, vie, liberté" ("Woman, Life, Freedom") with artists and academics to illustrate the 2022 protests in Iran following Mahsa Amini\'s death at the hands of morality police. Satrapi was elected to France\'s French Academy of Fine Arts in 2024 and declined the Legion of Honor award, citing insufficient support for Iranian democracy fighters. In January 2025, she wrote to French authorities that supporting the women\'s revolution in Iran requires more than just words or images. Satrapi won the Princess of Asturias Foundation award in Spain for communication and humanities in 2024, with the organization praising her as an "essential voice" in defending human rights and freedom.\n\nID: 4162114\nCREATED: 2026-06-05\nDOMAIN: apnews.com\nSLUG: marjane-satrapi-france-iran-artist-dies-5a731cded3163476aee9187aabe43113\nTEXT: Marjane Satrapi, a French-Iranian artist and filmmaker, has passed away. She was elected member of the French Academy of Fine Arts in 2024 and won the Princess of Asturias Foundation award in Spain for communication and humanities that same year. Satrapi coordinated the book "Femme, vie, liberté" with a group of artists and academics in 2023 to illustrate the revolts that occurred in Iran after Mahsa Amini\'s death. She declined France\'s highest award, the Legion of Honor, in 2024 due to concerns over supporting Iranian people fighting for democracy.\n\n\n',)
